{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he gave him.</b> King of Salem to Abraham — a tithe of all. <b>King of Salem</b> was removed from the priesthood and it was given to Abraham, because Abraham preceded to bless HaShem, as it is written: 'HaShem has sworn and will not relent: you are a priest forever, on the authority of Melchizedek.' And if you interpret the reverse, that Abraham gave the tithe to King of Salem, you would be saying that Abraham kept spoil for himself, when he himself already said: 'from a thread to a sandal strap,' etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:12.244942353Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}